;; This repository is a Guix channel: `uconsole/kernel.scm` and
;; `uconsole/system.scm` are modules you can import, with no -L plumbing and no
;; file copying. (Board firmware is not here: the system imports the platform's
;; `(rpi firmware)`.)
;;
;; DEPENDENCIES, and neither is optional. (uconsole kernel) imports (rpi kernel)
;; for the kernel construction, and those modules import (nongnu packages linux)
;; for linux-firmware, which carries the board's radio firmware. A channel whose
;; modules import an undeclared channel cannot even be COMPILED: it fails during
;; the checkout with "no code for module …". Declaring both here means
;; `guix pull`/`time-machine` fetch them for you, at these exact commits.
;;
;; Written as DATA, not as a (make-channel-introduction …) call: a dependency
;; inside .guix-channel is read with `read' and parsed by
;; `sexp->channel-introduction', which accepts only this shape. A call form
;; makes guix stop with "channel dependency has an invalid introduction field",
;; and a quoted name fails on symbol->string.
(channel
 (version 0)
 (dependencies
  (channel
   (name nonguix)
   (url "https://gitlab.com/nonguix/nonguix.git")
   (branch "master")
   (commit "6c2d4c89947e4fa381c896a204ee6bc5e81a7b8d")
   (introduction
    (channel-introduction
     (version 0)
     (commit "897c1a470da759236cc11798f4e0a5f7d4d59fbc")
     (signer "2A39 3FFF 68F4 EF7A 3D29  12AF 6F51 20A0 22FB B2D5"))))
  ;; The Raspberry Pi platform: the kernel constructor, the firmware packages and
  ;; the boot-chain tool this board layer builds on.
  ;;
  ;; The pin is the platform tree this board layer was split against: the kernel
  ;; constructor (rpi kernel), the no-op bootloader record (rpi bootloader), the
  ;; board-independent firmware (rpi firmware), the boot writer
  ;; (rpi-boot-populate) and the image builder (rpi image). A local checkout is
  ;; substituted by URL in the channels file; the commit stays.
  ;;
  ;; That commit carries the boot writer's --config-extra, which is how the board
  ;; half of config.txt is appended (uconsole/boot/config.txt), and the
  ;; (rpi bootloader) module this system declares. Moving the pin below the
  ;; first of those would break this board's config.txt half; moving it below
  ;; the second would not compile (uconsole system).
  (channel
   (name guix-raspberry-pi)
   (url "https://github.com/gortium/guix-raspberry-pi.git")
   (branch "main")
   (commit "9c31e14336df31dd2a27625e094253d5552ed4cf"))))
